---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import { getProjectTrackerSnapshot } from '../lib/projectTracker';

const tracker = await getProjectTrackerSnapshot();
const heroActions = [
	{ href: '/library', label: 'Browse the library', primary: true },
	{ href: '/presentations', label: 'Open presentations' },
	{ href: '/theory', label: 'Read the theory map' },
	{ href: '/program', label: 'See the program status' },
];

const highlights = [
	{
		tag: 'Core Claim',
		title: 'Adaptive Coherence Principle',
		copy:
			'Future-bearing systems persist only inside a nondegenerate interval between dissolution and total crystallization.',
	},
	{
		tag: 'Main Result',
		title: 'Crystallization Drift Theorem',
		copy:
			'The same self-reinforcing mechanisms that keep a system alive also push it toward organizational closure.',
	},
	{
		tag: 'Unification',
		title: 'Cross-domain reductions',
		copy:
			'The program derives dissipative structures, edge-of-chaos dynamics, free energy minimization, quantum Darwinism, information bounds, and Price/Fisher selection as special cases.',
	},
];

const architecture = [
	{
		title: 'Paper',
		copy:
			'The working manuscript states the ACP, proves the CDT, and packages the cross-domain story into a single theory spine.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Proofs',
		copy:
			'Standalone proof documents hold the core theorem chain, the coherent steering derivation, and the newer meta-theoretic coherence work.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Bridges',
		copy:
			'Bridge documents translate the theory into empirical predictions, Schur-complement structure, coordination floors, and arithmetic/operator regimes.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Research',
		copy:
			'Research notes and literature surveys track where the ACP, CDT, restraint-power, and vulnerable-margin claims already rhyme with established results.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Simulations',
		copy:
			'The simulation layer holds empirical prototypes and calibration tooling for testing whether the structural predictions leave measurable signatures.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Presentations',
		copy:
			'A dedicated public layer now exists for decks, whiteboards, and storytelling slide sequences built from PDFs and exported slide images.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Reductions',
		copy:
			'Formal reductions show how familiar results from separate literatures instantiate the same structural law under domain-specific variables.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Essays',
		copy:
			'Companion essays provide the philosophical frame and help translate the theory for readers outside the formal proof track.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Open Problems',
		copy:
			'The project keeps a live tracker of what remains unsolved, especially around coherence crisis dynamics, operator bridges, and empirical test design.',
	},
];

const currentSignals = [
	{ value: tracker.activePaperVersion, label: 'Current internal paper draft' },
	{ value: `${tracker.activeFrontCount}`, label: 'Active fronts in the live tracker' },
	{ value: `${tracker.openProblemCount}`, label: 'Open problems currently tracked' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="Adaptive Coherence Principle | Persistence Through Coherent Openness"
	description="A public-facing research site for the Adaptive Coherence Principle: the narrow interval where order and openness can survive together."
>
	<PageHero
		eyebrow="Research program"
		title="Adaptive Coherence Principle."
		asideTitle="What this project is"
		actions={heroActions}
		stats={currentSignals}
	>
		<p slot="copy">
			<strong>Adaptive Coherence Principle</strong> formalizes the claim that
			persistent systems survive by keeping enough order to remain coherent and
			enough openness to keep generating real futures.
		</p>

		<p slot="sidebar">
			This project is about the kind of truth that only exists in tension: too much
			certainty kills it, too little structure dissolves it. Faith, science, reason,
			love, and reality itself all seem to survive in the same narrow interval.
		</p>

		<div slot="sidebar" class="dense">
			<div>
				<strong>Current emphasis</strong>
				<p>Clarify the theory spine, map the research architecture, and expose the active fronts.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<strong>Recent additions</strong>
				<p>Control-theory bridge, Prediction 9 pilots, partition selectors, and meta-theoretic coherence.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<strong>Tracker freshness</strong>
				<p><code>STATUS.md</code> last updated {tracker.lastUpdated}.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</PageHero>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="license-callout">
			<div>
				<strong>CC0: take the ideas with you.</strong>
				<p>
					This project is intentionally released with no-strings-attached reuse in
					mind, so readers can carry the insights into their own frameworks and
					projects.
				</p>
			</div>
			<a class="button primary" href="/cc0">Why CC0</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<SectionHead
			kicker="Core structure"
			title="The productive interval"
			intro="The project’s central intuition is simple and severe: systems that remain capable of meaningful change must avoid two absorbing boundaries at once."
		/>

		<div class="interval-grid">
			<article class="interval-card">
				<h3>Dissolution</h3>
				<p class="subtle">
					Maximum entropy erases coherent structure. The system loses the ability to
					sustain a future-bearing trajectory.
				</p>
				<ul class="mini-list">
					<li>Thermodynamic equilibrium</li>
					<li>Loss of organized distinctions</li>
					<li>Death by dispersion</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="interval-card featured">
				<h3>Persistence interval</h3>
				<p class="subtle">
					The live regime is neither random nor fully closed. It keeps enough order to
					cohere and enough openness to continue generating new macroscopic futures.
				</p>
				<ul class="mini-list">
					<li>Nonzero conditional macrostate entropy</li>
					<li>Stability without lock-in</li>
					<li>Persistence as active maintenance</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="interval-card">
				<h3>Crystallization</h3>
				<p class="subtle">
					Total internal closure kills the future by removing real alternatives. The
					system remains, but its open-ended becoming does not.
				</p>
				<ul class="mini-list">
					<li>Zero conditional macrostate entropy</li>
					<li>Pathological lock-in and overfit</li>
					<li>Death by stasis</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<SectionHead
			kicker="What the program proves"
			title="One theory spine, several fronts"
		/>

		<div class="card-grid">
			{
				highlights.map((item) => (
					<article class="card">
						<span class="tag">{item.tag}</span>
						<h3>{item.title}</h3>
						<p>{item.copy}</p>
					</article>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="pillars">
			<div class="callout">
				<strong>Why it matters</strong>
				<p>
					If the theory holds, the pressure toward rigidity is not an accidental flaw
					of successful systems. It is a structural consequence of the same mechanisms
					that protect them from collapse.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="quote">
				The mechanisms that prevent dissolution are the same mechanisms that drive a
				system toward crystallization.
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<SectionHead
			kicker="Research architecture"
			title="The workspace is already shaped like a program"
			intro="The formalization is organized as a living research environment rather than a single manuscript folder. That makes the site a natural next layer, not a separate project universe."
		/>

		<div class="card-grid">
			{
				architecture.map((item) => (
					<article class="card">
						<h3>{item.title}</h3>
						<p>{item.copy}</p>
					</article>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="strip">
			<p>
				The site now has a real reading layer. The next clean iteration is to add
				search, cross-links, and curated pathways through the paper, proofs,
				reductions, and essays while keeping <code>Formalization/</code> as the
				source-of-truth research layer.
			</p>
			<a class="button primary" href="/library">Open the library</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
